    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -564.6010424426709,
        -453.32262885638954
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        720
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "READ ME - ALPHA-T1",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.33.1",
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# ALPHA-T1  -  single-pass MiniMax H3 i2v\n\nThe whole thing in one H3 pass. No LTX, no upscaler, no second sampler. This is the config\nthat rendered a 7 s clip at 704x384 in ~166 s with coherent motion and native audio.\n\n## Use\n1. Drop a still into **First frame**.\n2. Write the prompt in H3's template (positive box shows the shape: one referenced first\n   frame, ONE action with timed beats, an explicit camera contract, then soundscape).\n3. Set **Duration** (seconds); the math node snaps it to H3's 17k+5 frame law at 24 fps.\n4. **Resolution** = the only quality/speed dial. Turn it up for more pixels in the same\n   single pass:\n     - 0.27 MP = 704x384   (~166 s)  <- default, the fast one\n     - 0.4  MP = 864x480\n     - 0.6  MP = 1056x576\n     - 0.98 MP = 1344x768  (H3's ceiling)\n5. Queue. Output lands in `output/video/ALPHA-T1/` as mp4 with audio.\n\n## Baked in (leave alone)\neuler + bong_tangent, **12 steps**, CFG 1, turbo LoRA @ 0.5, FusedModulation + Sol-Attn\n(tau 1.3, min_tokens 4096, exact_kv). Seed is fixed at 757358688076805 - randomize it for\nvariety.\n\nThe lesson from the SA / LTX experiments: the motion and composition are entirely in this\none pass. A second pass (LTX refine or H3 2x upscale) only adds pixels, and costs far more\nthan just turning the resolution dial here.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# ALPHA-T1  -  single-pass MiniMax H3 i2v\n\nThe whole thing in one H3 pass. No LTX, no upscaler, no second sampler. This is the config\nthat rendered a 7 s clip at 704x384 in ~166 s with coherent motion and native audio.\n\n## Use\n1. Drop a still into **First frame**.\n2. Write the prompt in H3's template (positive box shows the shape: one referenced first\n   frame, ONE action with timed beats, an explicit camera contract, then soundscape).\n3. Set **Duration** (seconds); the math node snaps it to H3's 17k+5 frame law at 24 fps.\n4. **Resolution** = the only quality/speed dial. Turn it up for more pixels in the same\n   single pass:\n     - 0.27 MP = 704x384   (~166 s)  <- default, the fast one\n     - 0.4  MP = 864x480\n     - 0.6  MP = 1056x576\n     - 0.98 MP = 1344x768  (H3's ceiling)\n5. Queue. Output lands in `output/video/ALPHA-T1/` as mp4 with audio.\n\n## Baked in (leave alone)\neuler + bong_tangent, **12 steps**, CFG 1, turbo LoRA @ 0.5, FusedModulation + Sol-Attn\n(tau 1.3, min_tokens 4096, exact_kv). Seed is fixed at 757358688076805 - randomize it for\nvariety.\n\nThe lesson from the SA / LTX experiments: the motion and composition are entirely in this\none pass. A second pass (LTX refine or H3 2x upscale) only adds pixels, and costs far more\nthan just turning the resolution dial here.\n"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
